title DAHL-J9r1 — Skate, consent is mutual, presence is never default (Season 3 opens)
prompt Read REMEMBER + the 1,024-round itinerary; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, approve own design rounds, double-seat visions, send each increment as its own signed round, STOP at custody gates.
think Seasons 1 (TACT) and 2 (Yield) stand complete across every agent-doable rung; the itinerary's next Lindy-first crux on the whole road is Season 3 (Commons, DAHL), Journey 9 (Skate) — a new domain, so the filling law asks a self-approved design read first.
think Wrote the exploration doc: Skate carries Pond's own customs trichotomy (place/hold/refuse) to the social border, where the resting verdict is the strictest. The crux is mutual-only consent — a link exists only when both keepers request it; a one-sided request holds, never links; visibility follows the link exactly, so presence is never default.
think Chose mutual-only over a follower graph deliberately — a one-directional follow would make A→B visible without B's word, presence by one keeper's default, exactly what the promise refuses. Kept r1 pure (no signing), mirroring entity_books r1 and commerce_trade r1 fixing their laws before signing.
think Built skate_circle.rye as a bounded state machine — a link is not stored but derived as two opposing requests, so the mutual-only law cannot be bypassed by writing a link directly. visible == linked is invariant-asserted so the rule has one source of truth.
obs First build failed — open() bound c with var but never mutated it; Zig asked for const. Fixed.
obs tame_style_check bit `) == error.` at four refusal seams in the selftest; bound each result to a const first (the entity_books idiom) — captured-in-assert is welcome, bare call-seam compare is not. GREEN after.
loom witness=dahl_j9_skate_circle_witness cases=6 result=GREEN
file active-designing/20260812-201611_dahl-journey9-skate-consent-first-exploration.md the self-approved design round opening Season 3, Journey 9
file pond/apps/skate_circle.rye the pure consent state machine — mutual-only links, presence never default, every refusal bounded
file tools/dahl_j9_skate_circle_witness.rish GREEN witness — 2 welcomes (mutual-only crux, presence-never-default) + 4 refusals
